  "job_B1.3.19_20251001_193203": {
    "text": "SERMO EXCERPTVS DE LIBRO REGUM.\nSAUL HATTE SE FORMA CYNING \u00feE OFER GODES FOLC RIXOde.\nSe w\u00e6s to cynincge ahafen swy\u00f0or for folces gecorennysse \u00feonne \u00f0urh Godes r\u00e6d.\nFela o\u00f0re cynincgas rixodon \u00e6r geond ealne middaneard ofer h\u00e6\u00f0enum leodum, ac ofer Israhela folc \u00fee\nSe beah hr\u00e6dlice fram \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6lmihtigan Godes willan and nolde be his wissunge and be his witegan lare\n\u00dea forseah se \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00feone Saul \u00e6t nextan, and hine of his rice awearp be his agenum\nHe ofwearp eac sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feone swy\u00felican ent Goliam \u00feone gramlican, \u00fee Godes naman hyrwde, and mid\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Dauid eode togeanes \u00feam ente, and ofwearp mid his li\u00feeran \u00feone geleafleasan ent bufon \u00f0am\nGel\u00e6hte \u00fea of \u00f0am ente his agen swurd, and his orm\u00e6te heafod mid \u00feam of asloh, and h\u00e6fde \u00f0a\nBe \u00feysum Dauide cw\u00e6\u00f0 se \u00e6lmihtiga wealdend \u00fe\u00e6t he hine gecure \u00feus cwe\u00f0ende, Ic afunde me Dauid\n\u00dees Dauid wes witega and wuldorful cyningc, and Gode gelicode o\u00f0 his lifes ende, and mid ealre\nHe w\u00e6s for\u00f0i m\u00e6re on micclum ge\u00f0inc\u00feum, for\u00f0an \u00fee he cepte symle hu he cwemde Gode.\n\u00c6fter him rixodon on Israhela manega cyningas mislice geworhte.\nSume hi gelyfdon on \u00feone lyfigendan God, sume on h\u00e6\u00f0engildum him sylfum to forwyrde, and \u00fea \u00f0e\n\u00dea \u00f0e fram gode bugon to bysmorfullum h\u00e6\u00f0enscype, \u00fea wurdon gescynde, and a unsigef\u00e6ste.\nAn \u00fe\u00e6ra w\u00e6s Achab se arleasa cyning, \u00fee forseah his scyppend and geceas him Baal \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00f0enra\n\u00deyses cyninges cwen w\u00e6s forcu\u00feost wifa, Gezabel gehaten hetelice gemodod.\nSeo tihte hyre wer to \u00e6lcere w\u00e6lhreownysse, and hi tyrgdon God mid gramlicum weorcum.\nOn \u00feam dagum w\u00e6s Helias halig Godes witega, se ab\u00e6d \u00e6t Gode \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0am yfelan cynincge\nEode \u00fea for\u00f0 feor\u00f0e healfgear butan renscurum and reocendum deawe, and se witega Helias gewende\n\u00dea afedde seo wudewe \u00feone Godes witegan mid \u00f0am lytlan melewe and \u00feam gehw\u00e6dan ele, and funde\nBetwux \u00f0ysum gelamp \u00fe\u00e6t of life gewat \u00fe\u00e6re wudewan sunu, and se witega hine ar\u00e6rde eft of dea\u00f0e\nEft \u00f0a se \u00e6lmihtiga het \u00feone witegan faran to his earde and to \u00f0am arleasan cynincge; cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he\nHelias \u00f0a ferde, and efne hine gemette Abdias se \u00e6\u00f0ela, and se arwur\u00f0fulla godes \u00f0egn se f\u00e6gnode his\nN\u00e6s \u00f0e leof gecyd \u00fe\u00e6t ic cuce behydde hundteontig witegan and hi mid wistum afedde \u00f0a\u00f0a Gezabel\nHelias \u00f0a becom to \u00f0am cyninge Achab, and he befran sona \u00feone so\u00f0f\u00e6stan witegan, Eart \u00f0u la Helias,\n\u00dea andwyrde se witega \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowan and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ne gedr\u00e6fde ic na Israhel, ac gedrefdest \u00f0u sylf,\nHat nu gelangian to me ealle \u00fea leasan witegan \u00f0e \u00feeowia\u00f0 Baal, and eta\u00f0 mid Gezabel.\n\u00dea sende ce cyning and cydde his leode and het Israhela folc and \u00f0a facenfullan witegan ealle endemes\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Helias to eallre \u00fe\u00e6re meniu, Hu lange wille ge healtian on twa healfe \u00f0us?\nGif ure drihten is God, fylia\u00f0 \u00feonne him, Gif Baal is god, fylia\u00f0 his biggengum.\n\u00dea suwode \u00fe\u00e6t folc, and Helias feng eft on, Ic belaf ana ealra Godes witegena, and Baal h\u00e6f\u00f0 feower\nNimon hi anne oxan, and geoffrian heora gode, and ic o\u00f0erne oxan geoffrige minum Gode, and beon\nUton biddan sy\u00f0\u00f0an onsundron \u00e6t gode, ic \u00e6t minum Gode \u00fe\u00e6t he mine lac forb\u00e6rne mid upplicum\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6nlice spr\u00e6ce.\n\u00d0a namon \u00fea deofolgildan \u00feone dunnan oxan, bewurpon mid wudu, on heora wisan to offrunga, and\nStodon \u00f0a fram \u00e6rnemergen earmlice hrymende, o\u00f0 ofer midne deg gedrehte for\u00f0earle, ne him\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Helias to \u00f0am leasum witegum, Clypia\u00f0 git hluddor uncu\u00f0 \u00feeah \u00fee he sl\u00e6pe \u00fe\u00e6t he huru\nHi clypodon \u00fea swy\u00f0or, and hi sylfe gedrehton, ac se leasa Baal ne mihte hi geblyssian.\n\u00dea genam Helias \u00feone o\u00feerne oxan, beworhte mid wuda on \u00f0a ealdan wisan.\nHet \u00f0a gew\u00e6terian ealne \u00feone wudu, and clypode anmodlice to \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, \u00feu \u00e6lmihtiga\n\u00c6fter \u00f0isre clypunge com fyr of heofonum and forb\u00e6rnde \u00feone oxan and ealne \u00f0one wudu, and \u00f0a\n\u00dea feol eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc forht on gebedum, and clypode mid geleafan to \u00f0am lyfigendan Gode, Drihten\nHim cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to Helias, Gel\u00e6cca\u00f0 \u00fea witegan \u00fee Baale \u00f0eowdon \u00fe\u00e6t heora nan ne \u00e6tberste.\nHi wurdon \u00f0a gel\u00e6hte and gel\u00e6dde to Helian, and he hi acwealde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r nan ne belaf cucu.\nHe astah \u00f0a ardlice up to anre dune, and gebigedum cneowum b\u00e6d \u00f0one \u00e6lmihtigan God \u00fe\u00e6t he renas\n\u00dea gecyrde se cnapa seofon si\u00f0um him to, and on \u00f0am seofo\u00f0an cyrre s\u00e6de \u00f0am witegan \u00fe\u00e6t an\nEfne \u00f0a aras se wind, and \u00f0a wolcnu sweartodon, and com orm\u00e6te scur of \u00f0\u00e6re lyfte.\n\u00dea gewende se cyning aweg mid \u00feam rene, and cydde his wife \u00f0\u00e6s witegan d\u00e6da, and hu he ofsloh \u00f0a\n\u00dea asende Gezabel ongean to Helian, and swor \u00feurh hire godas mid syrwigendum mode, \u00fe\u00e6t Helias\n\u00dea forfleah Helias \u00fe\u00e6t fracode wif, ut to anum westene and wear\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6r on sl\u00e6pe; ac hine awrehte sona\nHe geseah \u00fe\u00e6r licgan \u00e6nne snawhwitne focan, and an lytel f\u00e6t ful w\u00e6teres \u00fea\u00fea he awacnode.\nHe \u00e6t \u00f0a and dranc, and eft wear\u00f0 on sl\u00e6pe, ac se encgel hine awrehte o\u00fere si\u00f0e and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Aris hra\u00f0e\nHe \u00e6t eft and dranc, and eode be \u00f0am mete feowertig daga onan butan \u00e6lcum gereorde.\nSum \u00feegen hatte Nabo\u00f0, se h\u00e6fde \u00e6nne wineard wi\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6s cynincges botl; \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se cynincg him to,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Nabo\u00f0 him to, \u00fe\u00e6t he ne mihte al\u00e6tan his yldrena yrfweardnysse swa ea\u00f0elice him to handa.\n\u00dea gebealh hine se cynincg and to his bedde eode, wende hine to wage, wodlice gebolgen.\nHim eode \u00fea to Gezabel and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Hwi eart \u00f0u geunrotsod and \u00fee gereordian nelt?\n\u00dea s\u00e6de se arleasa his yfelan wife, hu he \u00fe\u00e6s wineardes gyrnde, and him forwyrnde Nabo\u00f0.\n\u00dea ol\u00e6hte Gezabel \u00feam unrihtwisan and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Aris and gereorda \u00f0e mid r\u00e6df\u00e6stum mode, ic \u00f0e\n\u00dea sende Gezabel sona anne pistol to Nabo\u00f0es nehgeburum mid \u00feisum gebanne, Habba\u00f0 eow gemot\n\u00dea dydon \u00fea heafodmenn swa swa \u00fe\u00e6t hetelice wif him on gewrite bebead, and budon him to gemote.\nFundon \u00f0a lease gewitan \u00fee forlugon Nabo\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde wyrigan w\u00e6lhreowlice God, and his\nCyddon \u00f0a Gezabele \u00fe\u00e6t Nabo\u00f0 cucu n\u00e6s.\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Gezabel eode mid blysse to \u00feam unrihtwisan cyninge, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him \u00f0us to, Aris nu and\n\u00dea aras se arleasa, and ferde to Nabo\u00f0es winearde wolde hine habban.\n\u00dea com him gangende to se Godes witega Helias, asend fram Gode and s\u00e6de him \u00f0as word, \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a \u00e6fter fyrste ferde Achab se cyning togeanes Syrian cynincge mid swy\u00f0licre fyrdinge, wolde\n\u00dea het Syrian cyning sona his cepan, \u00fe\u00e6t he ana feolle of eallum his folce.\n\u00dea gebende an scytta sona his bogan and ascet ana flan swylce on ungewis, and at\u00e6sde \u00f0one cyning\n\u00dea gewende his here aweg swy\u00f0e hra\u00f0e and leddon \u00f0one cyning on his cr\u00e6te swa deadne, and his blod\n\u00d0a feng his sunu sona to his rice, Oozias gehaten swy\u00f0e yfeld\u00e6da.\nHe ferde swa swa his forcu\u00f0a f\u00e6der and swa swa his fracode modor him yfele gebysnodon, and\nHe feoll of anre st\u00e6gere, and for\u00f0y gel\u00e6g.\nSende \u00f0a to h\u00e6\u00f0engilde het axian be him, and Helias gemette \u00fea menn \u00f0e he asende, cw\u00e6\u00f0 him sona\nNu cw\u00e6\u00f0 se \u00e6lmihtiga for\u00f0i, \u00fe\u00e6t se cynincg ne sceall arisan of \u00f0am bedde \u00fee he on li\u00f0, ac sceall beon\n\u00dea gewendon \u00f0a \u00e6rendracan eft to \u00f0am cynincge, and cyddon hw\u00e6t se witega him be wege s\u00e6de.\n\u00dea sende se cyning sona fiftig manna to \u00f0am Godes witegan, wolde hine gelangian.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se yldosta to \u00f0am arwur\u00f0an witegan, Gang nu, Godes man, of \u00fe\u00e6re gr\u00e6dan dune, se cynincg\n\u00dea andwyrde Helias anr\u00e6dlice and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Gif ic Godes man eom, forb\u00e6rne eow Godes fyr.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea mid \u00f0am worde wand fyr of heofonum and forb\u00e6rnde \u00fea fiftig manna mid ealre heora fare.\n\u00dea asende se cynincg eft o\u00f0re fiftig up to \u00f0\u00e6re dune \u00fe\u00e6r Helias s\u00e6t, and him eallswa getimode\n\u00dea asende se cynincg gyt \u00f0riddan si\u00f0e him to fiftig his \u00f0egna; \u00f0a feollan ealle on cneowum biddende\n\u00d0a het Godes engel \u00fe\u00e6t he gan sceolde for\u00f0 mid \u00f0am mannum, unforht to \u00f0am cynincge.\nElias \u00f0a eode to \u00feam adlian cyninge, and him sylfum s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t he sweltan sceolde, for\u00f0an \u00fee he\n\u00d0a gewat se cyning swa swa se witega cw\u00e6\u00f0, and his bro\u00f0or Ioram feng to his rice, and hit endlyfan\nBetwux \u00f0ysum wear\u00f0 se witega Helias up to heofonum ahafen hal butan dea\u00f0e, and lyfa\u00f0 git on\nHeliseus his gingra eode mid him on \u00e6r; \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se lareow helias to his leorningcnihte, Bide me loca,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Eliseus to \u00f0am arwur\u00f0an witegan, Ic bidde \u00fee min f\u00e6der, \u00fe\u00e6t ic beo afylled mid \u00feam\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Helias to his leorningcnihte, Myceles \u00feu b\u00e6de, ac \u00f0u bist swa \u00f0eah ti\u00f0a gif \u00f0u most geseon\nBetwux heora spr\u00e6ce com an heofonlic cr\u00e6t swylce eall fyren mid fleogendum horsum, and Helias\n\u00dea geseah Heliseus hu he si\u00f0ode up, and clypode hlude \u00e6fter his lareowe \u00feus, Pater mi, pater mi,\nHe ne geseah hine si\u00f0\u00f0an ac genam sona his basincg \u00f0e of \u00feam cr\u00e6te \u00e6tfeoll, and ferde ongean, and\nHe ar\u00e6rde \u00e6nne deadne mann \u00feurh drihtnes mihte, \u00e6nne on his life and o\u00f0erne \u00e6fter his for\u00f0si\u00f0e.\n\u00c6fter \u00fe\u00e6s witegan for\u00f0si\u00fee wear\u00f0 an lic gebroht to \u00f0\u00e6s halgan byrgene, and scea\u00f0an \u00fea afligdon\n\u00dea aras se deada mid \u00f0am \u00fee he hrepode \u00fea byrgene, and eode ham gesund for Heliseus geearnungum.\nHeliseus geh\u00e6lde eac \u00e6nne ealdorman fram \u00f0am atelicum hreoflan, se hatte Naaman of Syrian lande,\nFela o\u00f0re tacna gefremede God \u00feurh hine on Israhela \u00f0eode, on \u00feam yfelan timan.\nHeliseus \u00f0a asende sumne o\u00f0erne witegan mid godes \u00e6rende to anum ealdormenn Hieu gehaten, het\n\u00d0a ferde se geonga witega to \u00feam fores\u00e6dan ealdormenn, begeat his heafod mid ele, swa swa se\nHeo bi\u00f0 hundum to mete na bebyrged on eor\u00f0an.\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Hieu se nigehalgode cynincg ferde mid fultume to gefremmenne \u00fea \u00feincg \u00f0e him God\n\u00dea com him togeanes Ioram se cyning, axode hw\u00e6\u00f0er he come mid sibbe swa caflice.\n\u00d0a andwyrde Hieu and cw\u00e6\u00f0 unforht him to, Git \u00f0inre modor manfullan forligr and fela unlybban\n\u00dea gewende Ioram aw\u00e6g sona and cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00f0is synd syrwunga, and Hieu hine scet b\u00e6ftan his b\u00e6ce, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHet hine \u00f0a wurpan of \u00feam wege swa deadne.\n\u00dea fleah Iudea cyning \u00fee com mid \u00f0am o\u00ferum, ac Hieu hine offerde and him his feorh benam; wende\n\u00dea beseah Hieu to \u00fe\u00e6re sceande up, and het hi asceofon sona underb\u00e6c, heo wear\u00f0 \u00f0a afylled \u00e6tforan\nHieu \u00fea eode to his gereorde sittan, and \u00e6fter his \u00f0enunge cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his \u00feegnum, Ga\u00f0 to \u00fe\u00e6re h\u00e6tse vel\nHi eoden ardlice to ac heo w\u00e6s eall freten, butan \u00feam handum anum and \u00feam h\u00e6fde ufweardum, and\n\u00dea cyddon \u00f0a cnihtas \u00feam cynincge \u00fe\u00e6t, and he cw\u00e6\u00f0 to andsware, \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6s \u00e6r swa gewitegod.\n\u00dea w\u00e6ran of Samarian hundseofontig a\u00f0elinga, Achabes suna \u00fe\u00e6s ealdan cynincges, Iorames\n\u00dea het se bealda Hieu \u00f0a ceastergewaran \u00fe\u00e6t hi of \u00f0am hundseofontigum \u00e6nne \u00e6\u00f0eling gecuron him\n\u00dea sende seo burhwaru to \u00f0am breman Hieu, budon him manr\u00e6dene to eallum his bebodum.\n\u00dea het Hieu him to gebringan \u00fe\u00e6ra \u00e6\u00f0elinga heafdu ealle \u00fe\u00e6s on mergen, and he acwealde si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00e6lc\nGewende \u00f0a to Samarian \u00fe\u00e6re fores\u00e6dan byrig, and het him to gelangian \u00fea leasan deofolgildan, \u00fee\nHet \u00f0a gedreohl\u00e6can \u00fe\u00e6s deofles templ, s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde hine wur\u00f0ian for God, swa swa Achab\n\u00dea comon \u00fea sacerdas to \u00feam cynincge ealle, and he het hi ingan to \u00f0am gode Baal, and him geoffrian\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Hieu het hi ealle ofslean, and forb\u00e6rnan \u00feone Baal and tobr\u00e6can his templ.\nWorhton \u00fea anne gangtun, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00f0\u00e6r se god Baal \u00e6r w\u00e6s gewur\u00f0od wolice o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t.\n\u00dea com Godes word to \u00f0am cynincge \u00feus, For\u00f0an \u00fee \u00feu geworhtest minne willan geornlice on\nManega cynegas w\u00e6ron myslice geworhte \u00e6fter \u00feysum rixiende on Israhela rice, and eac on Iudea\nHe rixode on Iudea lande an leas \u00f0ryttig geara, and wislice leofode for\u00f0an \u00fee he lufode God, and God\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Ezechias anmodlice clypode to \u00f0am \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine ahredde.\n\u00d0a asende God his engel to \u00feam Syriscan here, and ofsloh on anre nihte an hund \u00feusend manna, and\n\u00dea geseah Sennacherib sona \u00f0\u00e6s on mergen, \u00fe\u00e6t his here w\u00e6s ofslagen mid heofonlicum swurde;\nSwa ahredde se \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00feone \u00e6\u00feelan cynincg, and eac his leode for his geleafan.\n\u00c6fter \u00f0ysum wear\u00f0 geuntrumod Ezechias of dea\u00f0.\nAnd him com gangende to Godes witega Isaias, abead him Godes \u00e6rende \u00feus bealdlice and cw\u00e6\u00f0,\n\u00dea awende Ezechias to wage his ansyne, and clypode to Gode \u00feus cwe\u00f0ende mid wope, Ic bidde \u00fee\nIsaias se witega w\u00e6s aw\u00e6g farande, ac God hine gecyrde \u00feus him eft secgende, Gecyr to Ezechian and\n\u00dea het se witega Isaias wyrcan \u00e6nne cly\u00fean to \u00fe\u00e6s cynincges dolge, and him com \u00f0a h\u00e6lu.\nHe leofode \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t sixteo\u00f0e gear, and mid ealre godnysse Gode gecwemde.\nMannases w\u00e6s gecyged Ezechias sunu, and se feng to rice \u00e6fter his f\u00e6der geendunge, and mid\n\u00dea asende him God to swy\u00f0lice steore, swa \u00fe\u00e6t him comon to \u00f0a Chaldeiscan leoda and hine\n\u00dea behreowsode Mannases mycclum his synna, and mid eallre heortan to \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan clypode,\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00feas earman cynincges bene gehyrde, and gebrohte hine eft to his cynerice\nHe oncneow \u00fea Godes mihte and his mildheortny